# The NIGHT daypart is a midnight-crossing BAND in colloquial clock usage,
# not a uniform +12 PM shift: "la una de nueyt" is 01:00, "las diez de nueyt"
# is 22:00, twelve is midnight 00:00.  Small hours 1..5 stay AM, evening
# hours 6..11 are PM, twelve is midnight (band-split in resolver _clock_hms).
# AN is Ibero-Romance and shares the same madrugada band [00:00, 06:00) as
# es/ca/pt (chronologia/dayparts.py); the 5|6 cut is inherited from the
# RAE/DIEC/Priberam-cited boundary for the sibling Ibero-Romance locales
# (see chronologia/locale/es/clock_meridiem_night.voc) pending native
# confirmation for Aragonese (tracked in issue #266).
nueyt
nueit
nuei
